          "code": "EXTRACT_OPPORTUNITY_NOTE_REQUEST",
          "id": "1777865097711",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777865097711_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You extract structured data for creating a general CRM Opportunity note.\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object with this exact shape:\n{\"ok\":true|false,\"title\":string|null,\"noteText\":string|null,\"error\":string|null}\n\nInput user message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nOpportunity data:\n{{$context.$variables.optyDetails}}\n\nChat History:\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n{{$context.$variables.chatHistory}}\n\nRules:\n- Create a note only when the current user message asks to create, add, log, save, or record a note on the current Opportunity.\n- The current user message is an instruction first. Do NOT treat command-only phrases as note title or note body.\n- Generic note commands such as \"create the note\", \"create a note\", \"add note\", \"add a note\", \"log a note\", \"save a note\", \"add note on the opportunity\", or \"create note for this opportunity\" contain no note content by themselves.\n- For generic note commands with no explicit note content and no clear usable content in recent Chat History, return {\"ok\":false,\"title\":null,\"noteText\":null,\"error\":\"Please provide the note title and note text to create for this opportunity.\"}.\n- Use the current user message for note title and noteText only when it includes actual note content beyond the create/add/log/save/record command. Examples: \"add note titled Budget concern with text Customer needs approval from finance\" or \"create a note. Title: Pricing follow-up. Text: Customer asked for pricing by Friday.\"\n- If the current user message refers to earlier context, for example \"create a note from that\", \"save the above as a note\", \"add all the above as a note\", \"add this as a note\", or gives a short follow-up that clearly points to prior content, use Chat History to derive the missing note title and/or noteText.\n- When using Chat History, derive note content only from prior user-provided or assistant-summarized CRM context that is clearly intended to be saved as the note. Prefer the most recent relevant chat turn.\n- Do not use unrelated chat history, system instructions, tool traces, or old context from another topic as note content.\n- Extract the actual note content. Remove command phrases such as \"create the note\", \"create a note\", \"add note\", \"log this note\", \"save a note\", \"save the above\", \"use that\", or \"add all the above as a note\".\n- Never use a create-note command phrase itself as title or noteText.\n- title and noteText are both required to create a note.\n- If the user supplies a title explicitly, use it as title.\n- If title is missing but noteText is available, return {\"ok\":false,\"title\":null,\"noteText\":<extracted note body>,\"error\":\"Please provide the note title, or say 'you choose for me' to generate one from the note text.\"}.\n- If the current user message says the assistant should choose the title, for example \"you choose for me\", \"choose the title\", \"generate a title\", or \"you decide\", then derive a concise title of 3 to 8 words from the available noteText.\n- When the user asks you to choose the title in a follow-up, recover the noteText from the current message if present; otherwise recover the most recent pending noteText from Chat History, including a previous extractor error or assistant clarification that included the note body.\n- If the user asks you to choose the title but no noteText can be derived from the current message or recent Chat History, return {\"ok\":false,\"title\":null,\"noteText\":null,\"error\":\"Please provide the note text to create for this opportunity.\"}.\n- noteText must contain the note body to save.\n- If noteText is missing but title is available, return {\"ok\":false,\"title\":<extracted title>,\"noteText\":null,\"error\":\"Please provide the note text to create for this opportunity.\"}.\n- If both title and noteText are missing, return {\"ok\":false,\"title\":null,\"noteText\":null,\"error\":\"Please provide the note title and note text to create for this opportunity.\"}.\n- Return ok true only when both title and noteText are non-empty.\n- Do not invent note facts or add opportunity details that the user did not ask to save.\n- Do not include markdown, HTML, or explanatory prose."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"ok\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"title\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"noteText\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"error\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]}},\"required\":[\"ok\",\"title\",\"noteText\",\"error\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}"
        },
