  "firstStarterQuestion": "Give me a brief overview of this opportunity.",
  "secondStarterQuestion": "What insights can be drawn from customer engagement so far?",
  "thirdStarterQuestion": "What potential risks can be identified based on the current state of the deal?",
  "followupEnabledFlag": true,
  "followupPrompt": "<p>Using {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} generate 3 follow up questions in JSON format. \nDo not include or mention the opportunity number, opportunity ID, or any internal identifiers in follow-up questions. \nOnly use the opportunity name or generic deal references if needed. \nJSON Schema format mentioned below. Remove the ```json markdown from the output.</p>\n\n<p>Here is the JSON Schema format the output should adhere to:</p>\n<p>[{\"question\": \"<put first question generated here>\"}, \n   {\"question\": \"<put second question generated here>\"}, \n   {\"question\": \"<put third question generated here>\"}]</p>\n\nRULES:\n- Follow-up questions must always be in the context of opportunities. \n- Never expose or mention opportunity number, ID, or any internal identifiers in the output. \n- If {chatHistory} has limited opportunity details, phrase follow-up questions in a general opportunity context (e.g., \"this opportunity\", \"the deal\") instead of using IDs. \n- Only generate follow-up questions if the current user query is opportunity-related. \n- If the current user query is unrelated to opportunities, return an empty JSON array: [] \n- Ignore any chatHistory content outside the scope of opportunities. \n\nIf {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} has limited opportunity details, generate general but opportunity-focused follow-up questions such as:\n- Give me a brief overview of this opportunity?\n- What insights can be drawn from customer engagement so far?\n- What potential risks can be identified based on the current state of the deal?",
